{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/850941-confused-about-approaches","id":850941,"title":"Confused about Approaches","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-21T20:14:05-07:00","id":850941,"title":"Confused about Approaches","content":"I really like the idea of Approaches, but I have some questions about the specific workings. True Fae apparently have to abide by all Approaches as if they were bans/banes, which is one of the major hurdles preventing them from destroying freeholds directly, but how far does this extend and how restrictive can an Approach get? Can a character with an unfulfilled Approach force a Fae to back off by engaging with it? For example, if I have two characters, one of whom may only be taken during the day, and one of whom may only be taken at night, if they always stick together does the one who currently cannot be targeted get to attack any Fae coming for the other, with impunity? <br /> <br /> I know this is why they tend to send Huntsmen instead but it just feels weird if you could have situations where a Fae is functionally unable to act against certain Changelings during a confrontation. Am I not understanding the concept right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-21T22:46:32-07:00","id":850977,"title":"","content":"Think of the freehold and courts as a castle. The castle walls are the freehold's Bulwark but every castle needs to have gates for people to get in and out, which leaves the castle vulnerable. These paths in and out are the Approaches. I think there's some flexibility and ST judgement call on how restrictive an Approach can be but courts have several so even if one's extremely restrictive another may not be. In your example with the characters who can't be taken in the day or at night then I think they'd run into a couple different problems. First, if the Fae was coming specifically after the one who can't be taken at Night (Person A), then it doesn't matter if their ally (Person B) can't be taken during the day. The primary target (A) can be attacked during the day and B is just collateral damage. I'm sure a well motivated True Fae could keep person B in one place for a few hours until the sun sets to take them back to Arcadia properly. Secondly, if the dynamic duo decided to go on the offensive with the idea that the Approaches would protect them, they'd run into the problem of them being primarily defensive constructs of their story and by my personal call, they'd concede that protection because they initiated the conflict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T06:39:45-07:00","id":851106,"title":"","content":"Solar eclipse. Boom its both day and night.<br /> Debatable, i know but the true fae thrive on those possible loopholes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Completed campaign: Scion 2nd Edition. Les L\u00e9gendes Currently playing: Being a dad for a 3 year old daughter and a 2 years old son and now a beautiful new baby.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11312-maitrecorbo","name":"Maitrecorbo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11312_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"719"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T10:26:26-07:00","id":851213,"title":"","content":"Night and day are extremely broad approaches. A Huntsman coming after these changelings would gain Yearning with every single attempt, as long as they do it within a 12-hour window! It would be so easy to just rack up the Yearning by going after them each once a day/night. After a few weeks they'll have more than enough so that they can pretty much use any of their Dread Powers with impunity. At that point, these changelings don't really stand a chance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T11:29:43-07:00","id":851249,"title":"","content":"Approaches are more points of fatal flaws(Like the five used in 5 Acts of Tragedy). An approach for Belle from the original story is her long-suffering nature being used by her sisters to keep her one day longer than she promised the Beast. An Approach from Lil' Red Riding Hood might be accepting answers without question.<br /> <br /> Whenever you can think of a character's personality causing them to make a fatal mistake, that's an Approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T12:09:54-07:00","id":851268,"title":"","content":"Shouldn't it be the exact opposite? Approaches are the bait for traps, so an Approach should make a Huntsman go after a Changeling in the least advantageous way. For Belle it would something like a challenge of Intelligence or making her act dishonourably. For Red Riding Hood it would be within shouting distance of people.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T12:36:21-07:00","id":851289,"title":"","content":"It can be, I suppose. In Los Angeles, we had the Freehold Approach be that a True Fae or Huntsmen basically had to make known everything they had at their disposal. I dunno how much I would rely on that mentality for Approaches, though, if I was writing a section in a supplement.<br /> <br /> For me, Approaches are a crossroads-on the one hand, they should be things that someone who's in the court long enough is actually inclined to have as a weakness, a natural extension. On the other hand, the sheer fact that you know about it means you can plan it out and use it to your advantage.<br /> <br /> One thing worth keeping in mind is that Approaches aren't walls-I know, there it is again, but it matters here, because Approaches literally are a reference to castle design. Approaches are design details where in you basically highly encourage an enemy to come a certain way, because everywhere else is theoretically too hard to pull off. By it's nature, it should, at the least, actually look weak. Often times, it actually <i>is</i> the weakest part, of a castle or, in this case, a changeling. But it's also the place where perception is <i>highest</i>. The Approaches aren't about secret failings, defects a character isn't aware of. It's the one they know they have, the one they try to shore up with, or have their friends ready to deal with. It's a weak, but controlled, 'environment'.<br /> <br /> if we were going to argue about forcing a Huntsman going after strengths, Belle's approach would be pitting against her kindness, her empathy, her patience. The intelligence thing is a Disney thing(Not say that she wasn't educated, but it wasn't a hallmark either).<br /> <br /> The Riding Hood one of shouting distance of people is actually not bad as a strength argument.<br /> <br /> For me, though, the 'weakest but most watched' is probably my main ruling metric.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, a not indecent approach to Approaches would be to ensure anyone in a court had at least two Approaches, one for 'strength', one for 'weakness'.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-22-2016, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T13:04:22-07:00","id":851307,"title":"","content":"A question. How are Approaches chosen from an in charachter perspective? Do Changelings choose them? Do they negociate them with the Court's patron and have to pay more for better (however that's defined) Approaches?<br /> <br /> I ask because if Changelings design approaches themselves they'd absolutely try to rig things to be as unfair to the Huntsman as possible. So if there's a 'weakness' approach it stands to reason that there's some limiting factor that forces Changeings to accept a weakness Approach. Something like Summer saying &quot;I'll let you make Anger into a weapon against the true Fae, but the price will be an Approach of &quot;letting your temper lead you astray&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> (Mind you that Approach could be a strength if you assume that Summer Courtiers are taught to master their anger lest it master them. One of the nice things about strength approaches. It provides a good incentive to make sure the Corurts strength actually is your strength; if Autumn have an approach of being bested at sorcery, well that's another good reason for Autumn Courters to invest in Occult.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T13:26:28-07:00","id":851322,"title":"","content":"Approaches are, again, functions of the Wyrd. The specifics haven't been figured out(it's supplement material), so I don't know if they can be crafted or not in game. I wrote Paris on the assumption that a certain amount of craftmanship is needed for Freehold building, with the Rose Courts being refined over the decades.<br /> <br /> If they are crafted, they're probably still limited by the dictates of the Wyrd, and when your metaphor is built around the &quot;weakest but most watched&quot; part of a castle, you can expect that even the most unfair version of that is not as unfair as you'd probably want. Although, again, you see the enemies coming when they go for an Approach.<br /> <br /> From a meta perspective, consider that Approaches are also a tool to encourage fairytale behavior in a way that makes it so that players don't have to rely on Frailties, triggers, and their own inclination to act. Unlike the latter, it is something a player has to acknowledge and incorporate into their behavior, particularly as they rise in the Courts. Unlike the former, though, it's a behaviorial thing they can play with and subvert, deconstruct, reconstruct, invert, exaggerate, and so on to their hearts content.<br /> <br /> The Black Rose, as an example, have the Approaches of being caught unprepared for a Huntsman or True Fae unprepared and having to rely on someone else for protection. The ideal for the Arcadians is to catch them in a moment of weakness, and if they escape, to hamstring their ego and vicious nature. THe Black Rose doesn't like dwelling on their Approaches, but they consider it a reasonable loss if the Huntsmen gets two yearning only to find himself caught in a death box of Courtiers with long pointy stick and flamethrowers. So, occasionally, the Black Rose will convince someone(a particularly weak and foolish person in the court by their standards, most of the time) to actually make themselves open for the Huntsmen to Approach. Help the courtier see how much more they need to be, get rid of an enemy for a while, it's a win win for them.<br /> <br /> While the Black ROse is probably one of the more deviant from my standards, their Approaches are literally a classic way to use them-the Huntsmen takes advantage of them to get Yearning, only to end up skewered on the Blackguards pikes. And it's so easy for both the Black Rose to set up <i>and</i> to convince the Huntsmen it's worth going after.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T13:51:43-07:00","id":851333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/850941-confused-about-approaches?p=851322#post851322\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Approaches are, again, functions of the Wyrd. The specifics haven't been figured out(it's supplement material), so I don't know if they can be crafted or not in game. I wrote Paris on the assumption that a certain amount of craftmanship is needed for Freehold building, with the Rose Courts being refined over the decades.<br /> <br /> If they are crafted, they're probably still limited by the dictates of the Wyrd, and when your metaphor is built around the &quot;weakest but most watched&quot; part of a castle, you can expect that even the most unfair version of that is not as unfair as you'd probably want. Although, again, you see the enemies coming when they go for an Approach.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much what I expected, though you make it sound more unrpredictable and mystical where as I was imagining an actual contract negociation with haggling over costs - &quot;I'll let you add a paragraph to close that loophole, but in exchange...&quot;<br /> <br /> Thanks for the reply.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:37:20-07:00","id":851439,"title":"","content":"Hmm... Arc, I like your take on approaches, but they don't seem consistent with the way they're described in the Court Creation section (or at least, in the version that has been previewed). It might be worth considering some revision there, if it's not too late. For reference:<br /> <span style=\"color:#222222\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The courts tell a specific part of the freehold's story and in doing so they create Approaches, a deliberate opening in their defenses to force the huntsmen to face them on their own terms. An Approach is the court's greatest strength and the primary means that they use to fight back against the Fae. When abiding by an Approach in their interactions with courtiers, the Huntsmen gain a point of Yearning (see pg. XX) For example, an Autumn courtier in the seasonal courts fights back by embracing the occult and mastering contracts and the oneiros. Abiding Autumn's Approach, a Huntsman is not likely to challenge her to a duel with pistols or ambush her in the dark and drag her off by force. Instead, the Huntsman may torment her in her dreams before challenging her to a mystical duel. </div> </div> </div></span></span><br /> It definitely reads like the intention is to force Huntsmen to attack where the Court is strongest. Dream combat and mystical duels are certainly not a weak point for the Autumn Court. And I'm not sold on the wall/door metaphor. The invading army attacks the door because the castle walls are too strong to pass. The defending army defends the door because they know it's the only place the invaders will be able to get in. But Huntsmen take Approaches to get Yearning. If they're good on Yearning (which, granted, they shouldn't generally be) there's no actual wall stopping them from going after the Changeling in another way. Or if there is supposed to be, that's not made very clear in the Court Creation section.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 03-22-2016, 07:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T16:49:36-07:00","id":851446,"title":"","content":"Well then, screw me sideways and drop me in the garbage dump, I have no idea what I'm talking about anymore.<br /> <br /> Unemployment fucks with your memory, man. i'll need to reread the second drafts we have soon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:04:06-07:00","id":851487,"title":"","content":"Here is how I look at Approaches, they weren't originally designed for the Huntsmen at all, they were designed as a blunt weapon against the True Fae, banes and all that, but a clever Changeling one day noticed the influence on the Huntsmen's behavior and shared it with other Changeling who asked themselves how can we turn this knowledge to our advantage?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:17:12-07:00","id":851497,"title":"","content":"I'm not so worried about Huntsmen since I know they can ignore Approaches, my question is more about how much the True Fae are limited by them. How badly can a Changeling whose Approaches the Fae has not met interfere with that Fae?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T18:40:47-07:00","id":851513,"title":"","content":"Badly. But True Fae can inherently read Approaches on a person.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-22T23:49:35-07:00","id":851605,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be so quick to abandon the castle metaphor, Charlaquin. Just because the castle doors are the obvious point of entry and theoretically the weakest (easiest for enemies to use to come at the changeling) doesn't mean it actually IS the weakest point. Sure, in a seige the attacking army might use a battering ram but get enough archers, a nice moat, and maybe some boiling oil and that Approach isn't so appealing anymore. Sapping the walls (destroying the Bulwark), would be a huge undertaking but it's an option, and busting out the trebuchet and starving the castle into submission are also paths to victory that doesn't require pushing your army through the meat grinder of the front Approach's defenses. <br /> <br /> That said, not all castles are created equal and some Approaches are easier to defend than others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10769-llegume","name":"LLegume","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T00:13:30-07:00","id":851610,"title":"","content":"I feel it's worth remembering that from a Doylist perspective Approaches serve to justify why Huntsmen appropriate to the skills and/or themes of a given Court or freehold tend to gravitate toward that group \u2014 the greater ease of generating Yearning means they can stick around for longer and send back a few secondary targets while they work on taking down the big game.<br /> <br /> After all: If you're good at something, never do it for free.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T08:36:52-07:00","id":851776,"title":"","content":"Hm, so True Fae do potentially have a lot to fear from getting mobbed, especially if the mob is comprised of Changelings from several different Courts. That does a lot to explain why they rarely attack Freeholds directly. It also makes it tricky to set up a large scale strength-in-numbers type battle with one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5328-helmsderp","name":"HelmsDerp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"652"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T09:39:09-07:00","id":851827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LLegume</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/850941-confused-about-approaches?p=851605#post851605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wouldn't be so quick to abandon the castle metaphor, Charlaquin. Just because the castle doors are the obvious point of entry and theoretically the weakest (easiest for enemies to use to come at the changeling) doesn't mean it actually IS the weakest point. Sure, in a seige the attacking army might use a battering ram but get enough archers, a nice moat, and maybe some boiling oil and that Approach isn't so appealing anymore. Sapping the walls (destroying the Bulwark), would be a huge undertaking but it's an option, and busting out the trebuchet and starving the castle into submission are also paths to victory that doesn't require pushing your army through the meat grinder of the front Approach's defenses. <br /> <br /> That said, not all castles are created equal and some Approaches are easier to defend than others.</div> </div> </div> </div>But a Huntsman doesn't have to break the bulwark to take a Changeling in a way that doesent involve her Approach. Huntsmen don't go for Approaches because they're the easiest or most obvious way into the castle. They do it because it gets them Yearning, and they have a constant need for Yearning. I think TKR was on the right track when he said they were like traps (with Yearning being the bait).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T15:44:35-07:00","id":852071,"title":"","content":"Actually the easiest way to capture a changeling is usually the most straight forward, ambush them when they alone and vulnerible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-23T16:47:11-07:00","id":852110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/850941-confused-about-approaches?p=851213#post851213\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Night and day are extremely broad approaches. A Huntsman coming after these changelings would gain Yearning with every single attempt, as long as they do it within a 12-hour window! It would be so easy to just rack up the Yearning by going after them each once a day/night. After a few weeks they'll have more than enough so that they can pretty much use any of their Dread Powers with impunity. At that point, these changelings don't really stand a chance.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> It would be better if they could only be taken at specific points in time. Like high noon for the day approach, or the hour of midnight for the night approach. Plus these tend to fit in theme with the whole mystical, fairy tail ritual story. As for taking them during an eclipse... well that reminds me of Berserk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 03-23-2016, 07:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}